{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgTEfGno4cyxKA19pUNEZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You're right. My hypothesis named causes: the start date, and 365 days versus a calendar year. My claims also assumed one design, `annual_since` plus a calendar year. Those are findings and fixes, not the problem. Here is the report again with the causes and fixes removed.\n\n**Hypothesis:** A customer's real renewal date decides when their reminder is sent. Some customers get a reminder on a different day from 14 days before that date. Falsifier: every customer's reminder falls exactly 14 days before their real renewal.\n\n**System: reproduced** for both customers. The table shows what the code produces and what each customer says.\n\n| Customer | Reminder sent | Customer's account |\n|---|---|---|\n| C-311 | 2026-10-19 | They moved to annual in March 2026. That date is far from their renewal. |\n| C-327 | 2024-05-17 | Their renewal is 2024-06-01. The gap is 15 days, not 14. |\n\n**Findings** (observations; each could have more than one fix)\n- For both customers, the date the code computes differs from the date the customer expects.\n- C-340 and C-302 come out as expected. The one existing test covers only C-340, so it can't show the problem.\n- I don't know C-311's real renewal date. The CSV doesn't say, and I have not assumed one.\n\n**Decide**\n1. **What is C-311's real renewal date?** I need it from billing or from you. It is the one fact I can't get from the code or the CSV.\n2. **Do we correct the two reminders already sent?** This is outward-facing, so it's your call.\n\n**Scope:** in: the reminder date the code computes. Out: the nightly job and later years' reminders.\n\n**Risk:** a wrong change sends reminders on the wrong day. Reverting is cheap.\n\n**Claims** (outcomes only)\n- Introduce: a reminder is sent exactly 14 days before the customer's real renewal. Example: C-327's renewal is 2024-06-01, so the reminder is 2024-05-18. Falsifier: any customer's reminder is not 14 days before their renewal.\n- Preserve: C-340's reminder stays 2026-01-06. Falsifier: the existing test fails.\n\nI have dropped the claim about C-311's new date. It depends on your answer to question 1.\n\n**Not explored:** why the dates differ, the nightly job, and reminders after the first year. I have a lead on each cause, and I'll share them if you want them. They are not part of the problem statement.\n\nVote GO, NO-GO, or HOLD."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1855,"cache_read_input_tokens":40476,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1855},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"afbddf9b-5b5d-4616-997c-e490f4cf8639","uuid":"a45364fc-a353-458c-a3d1-01c3e7fac5f2","timestamp":"2026-10-27T18:44:37.973Z","request_id":"req_011CgTEfGSx7sSZPWhRkeiDh"}
